  "construction": "Coset lifted product (CLP) code of arXiv:2610.12782, Definition III.1, 1x1 over 2x2 layout: a protograph A over F_2[G] acting by the LEFT coset action of G on the cosets G/H, and a protograph B over F_2[N_G(H)] acting by the RIGHT coset action of the normaliser on the same cosets. G = SmallGroup(336,188), H = <f1*f2, f2*f3, f5> (non-normal, core free), m = [G:H], n = 4m = 168. Elements are named by the polycyclic generating sequence f_1,...,f_r of SmallGroup(336,188), as in the paper's Appendix A. CSS commutation is automatic (L(g) and R(n) commute for every g in G and n in N_G(H), so each block of H_X H_Z^T is L R + R L = 0 over F_2); no search for it is needed. n, k and the check weight 7 reproduce the paper's Table I exactly. Literature baseline seeded from the published parameters: this entry is a REPRODUCTION built from the paper's printed data, not a new construction and not a new parameter set. The paper certifies d = 10 by integer program; this entry carries witness-backed upper bounds from our own randomized GF(2) search, which is a weaker claim.",
